num += 1;
if (num [b]==[/b] 42) {
   printf("You won!");
}[/code]
An expression that evaluates to a non-zero value is considered true.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="c" codeId="1639"]int in_stock = 20;
[b]if (in_stock)[/b]
  printf("Order received.\n"); [/code]
