[s0l0!-header][h1]The if-else Statement[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The [b]if[/b] statement can include an optional [b]else[/b] clause that executes statements when an expression is [b]false[/b].
For example, the following program evaluates the expression and then executes the [b]else [/b]clause statement: [code format="c" codeId="1632"]#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
  int score = 89;
  
  [b]if [/b](score >= 90)
    printf("Top 10%%.\n");
  [b]else[/b]
    printf("Less than 90.\n");
    
  return 0;
}[/code]
[note]Run the code and see how it works![/note]

